# PR#380: real, known and not what this slice can fix. The webhook transport carries no
# ordering, which is what fazer-ai/chatwoot#373 records and what the job this finding
# names documents at its top: the payloads have nothing monotonic to rebuild an order
# from, so the only thing on offer is waiting, and waiting is what `:deferred` does for
# the case a target that is not stored yet. The remedy asked for here, serializing every
# event of a session or a chat, is a different inbound design (one queue per session, or
# a per-chat cursor with something to compare), not a change to this job. The reaction
# sub-case has a cheaper answer that is worse: deferring a removal that finds no active
# reaction would spend the whole retry ladder on every stray removal, which is the
# ordinary shape (a reaction taken back on a message from before the inbox was connected)
# in exchange for a race between two webhooks that are usually seconds apart.
